threads.body:
This comment doesn't match what the test actually guards against. Draining on the calling thread -- which is what the code did before this PR -- never deadlocks on large output; it just leaves the read unbounded. The deadlock only shows up if you wait for the process to exit before reading its output, which is what this test is really protecting against.

```suggestion
    // more output than fits in the pipe buffer: waiting for the process to exit before reading
    // its output would deadlock here
```

